lowpage_* -- the fixtures for `kuna xrefs` over an address formed from the
program counter below 0x1000, in images that map code or constants in their
first page (GH #1364; decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/xrefs_low_page.rs).

What they are
  lowpage_macho_arm64  arm64 Mach-O dylib (zero-based) from the issue's own
                       assembly plus adr, adrp + add of a __cstring literal and
                       adrp + ldr of a __TEXT,__const word, all below 0x400.
  lowpage_x86_64       x86-64 ELF shared object: lea [rip] of .rodata at 0x2a4.
  lowpage_rv64         RV64 ELF shared object: auipc + addi and auipc + lw of
                       .rodata at 0x2a0.
  lowpage_i386         i386 PIE: lea and mov through the GOT pointer that
                       __x86.get_pc_thunk.bx establishes, into .rodata at 0x170.
  lowpage_arm          ARM image linked at 0x100 (a firmware layout): A32 adr,
                       Thumb adr + ldr and Thumb adr.w.
  Each also has a control_number(s) function that builds the same addresses as
  plain immediates, which are numbers and must stay unreported.
  Sources: lowpage_macho.s, lowpage_<arch>.S, lowpage_arm.ld.

Why they are vendored
  They are assembled and linked for five foreign targets, and the property
  under test is the linker's layout (ld.lld puts .rodata in an ELF image's first
  page; a dylib's __TEXT starts at 0), so the binaries are checked in.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu clang 14.0.0 assembles; the rustup-bundled LLD 20.1.8 (rustc 1.90.0,
  lib/rustlib/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin/gcc-ld/{ld.lld,ld64.lld}) links:

      clang -target arm64-apple-macos11 -c lowpage_macho.s -o macho.o
      ld64.lld -dylib -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 11.0 \
          -fixup_chains -o lowpage_macho_arm64 macho.o
      clang -target x86_64-linux-gnu -c lowpage_x86_64.S -o x86_64.o
      ld.lld -shared --build-id=none --no-relax -o lowpage_x86_64 x86_64.o
      clang -target riscv64-linux-gnu -c lowpage_rv64.S -o rv64.o
      ld.lld -shared --build-id=none --no-relax -o lowpage_rv64 rv64.o
      clang -target i386-linux-gnu -c lowpage_i386.S -o i386.o
      ld.lld -pie --build-id=none -e audit_string -o lowpage_i386 i386.o
      clang -target armv7a-none-eabi -c lowpage_arm.S -o arm.o
      ld.lld -static -nostdlib -e main --build-id=none -T lowpage_arm.ld \
          -o lowpage_arm arm.o

  The controls' immediates are the linked addresses, so a source edit that
  moves a symbol needs them updated.

